- one to many (1:N)
- many to many (N:N)


#JOINS: connecting tables

Primary Key
    ↓
uniquely identifies a row

Foreign Key
    ↓
points to another table's row

JOIN
    ↓
uses that relationship to bring data together


NNER JOIN returns only the rows where there is a matching value between the two tables according to the ON condition.
SELECT
    stud.name,
    course.course
FROM stud
INNER JOIN course
ON stud.course_id = course.id;


2. LEFT JOIN: LEFT JOIN keeps every row from the LEFT table, even when there is no match in the right table.

SELECT
    stud.name,
    course.course
FROM stud
LEFT JOIN course
ON stud.course_id = course.id;


3.RIGHT JOIN: RIGHT JOIN keeps every row from the RIGHT table, even when there is no match in the LEFT table.

4. FULL join : GIVE EVERYTHING FROM BOTH TABLE
5. self join: A table joins with itself.